  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protected area conservation and survey of eastern chimpanzees, South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 2-year project is to protect eastern chimpanzees by working with the Ministry of Wildlife Conservation and Tourism (MWCT) in two game reserves of Gbudue State, South Sudan to establish baseline chimpanzee abundance and lay the groundwork for sustained monitoring. Specific activities include: 1) continuing development of anti-poaching presence in the reserves; 2) continuing to clarify, codify and demarcate the legal boundaries of the reserves and to identify adjoining areas deserving of protection; and 3) further documenting chimpanzee abundance through camera trap surveys.</narrative>
  </description>
